meta {
  name: Deny Request
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.putRecord
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "repo": "{{did}}",
    "collection": "app.bsky.graph.followRequest",
    "rkey": "{{followRequestRkey}}",
    "record": {
      "$type": "app.bsky.graph.followRequest",
      "subject": "{{targetDid}}",
      "status": "denied",
      "createdAt": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Deny Request
  
  Updates a follow request record status to "denied".
  
  ## Request Body
  - `repo` (string): Repository DID where the request record exists
  - `collection` (string): "app.bsky.graph.followRequest"
  - `rkey` (string): Record key of the follow request
  - `record` (object):
    - `$type`: "app.bsky.graph.followRequest"
    - `subject` (string): Target DID (same as original)
    - `status` (string): "denied"
    - `createdAt` (string): ISO 8601 timestamp
  
  ## Response
  Returns the updated record:
  - `uri`: AT URI of the follow request record
  - `cid`: Content ID of the updated record
  
  ## What Happens When Denied
  1. Follow request status is updated to "denied"
  2. No follow record is created
  3. The requester is NOT added to allowed followers
  4. The requester cannot view the private profile or content
  5. The requester can see the status in their outgoing requests
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Part of "Deny Request" workflow:
  1. Bob creates follow request to Alice
  2. Alice finds Bob's request (by listing or URI)
  3. Alice updates the request status to "denied"
  4. No follow record is created
  5. Bob is NOT added to Alice's allowed followers
  6. Bob cannot view Alice's private profile
  
  ## Follow-up Actions
  After denial, the requester:
  - Can see the request status is "denied" when listing their requests
  - Request may have cooldown period before resending (implementation dependent)
  
  **Environment Variables Required:**
  - `{{did}}`: DID of the repo owner (Bob's DID if Bob sent the request)
  - `{{followRequestRkey}}`: Record key from the follow request URI
  - `{{targetDid}}`: Alice's DID (the subject of the request)
}
